  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 102 AM MDT Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nTuesday - Saturday: For the remainder of the forecast period, active \nweather can be expected for south central and southeastern Colorado. \nWhile the Sunday-Monday storm system will be exiting the region \nthrough Tuesday, additional waves are anticipated to pass over the \narea through the week, which will bring brief periods of increased \nprecipitation chances and breezier winds. Any precipitation chances \nwill be greatest along the mountains, where forcing will be \nmaximized. With that all said, while confidence is high (60-70%) in \nthe unsettled pattern, uncertainty does still remain in how \nindividual waves will evolve given the messy pattern that develops. \nOtherwise, mostly clear to partly cloudy skies and fairly stable, \nand near seasonal, temperatures can be anticipated through the\nweek.",
